1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:04,346
For decades, scientists said Easter Island's statues were dragged on wooden sleds.

2
00:00:04,296 --> 00:00:05,694
But there's a problem.

3
00:00:05,694 --> 00:00:07,796
The island had almost no trees.

4
00:00:07,796 --> 00:00:10,407
The Rapa Nui people always had a different answer.

5
00:00:10,407 --> 00:00:11,953
The statues walked.

6
00:00:11,953 --> 00:00:14,824
In 2011, archaeologists tested it.

7
00:00:14,824 --> 00:00:16,203
18 people.

8
00:00:16,203 --> 00:00:17,518
3 ropes.

9
00:00:17,518 --> 00:00:19,222
A 5-ton replica.

10
00:00:19,222 --> 00:00:20,379
It walked.

11
00:00:20,379 --> 00:00:22,500
887 statues.

12
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:24,675
Moved up to 18 km.

13
00:00:24,675 --> 00:00:26,083
All by walking.

14
00:00:26,083 --> 00:00:28,694
The Rapa Nui told us the truth for centuries.

15
00:00:28,694 --> 00:00:30,185
We just didn't listen.

